implementationPlan.description:
stopSeat (DoD 4).
export stopSeat(input, steps = {}). input is exactly { project, owner, instance }, where instance passes isOwnedInstanceName; else SEAT_INPUT_INVALID. With provider = { executable: platform.executable }:
- If the record file ownedLedgerDir(project)/<instance>.json is absent (lstat ENOENT), resolve vm 'gone'. This is idempotent after a retire.
- Otherwise remove({ ledger, name: instance, owner, provider }), the real deleteOwned:
  - 'deleted', which deleteOwned also returns for an already-deleted record: vm 'deleted';
  - 'not-launched' on a reserved record: ledger.retire, vm 'retired';
  - collision: vm 'none' (foreign, untouched).
- LIFECYCLE_NOT_OWNER passes through, so another seat's record is never touched.
- Any other failure is SEAT_STOP_FAILED, and the record is kept.
It never lists, sweeps or touches any other record.
Test AS4. With two seat records A and B:
- stopSeat(A) deletes A, and every provider call names only A;
- a second stopSeat(A) gives 'deleted' with no provider delete call;
- after a retire it gives 'gone';
- stopSeat(B's instance, A's owner) gives LIFECYCLE_NOT_OWNER, and B is unchanged byte for byte;
- a failing provider delete gives SEAT_STOP_FAILED, with the record kept.
error handling: every result is one fixed code, never message text.
